 173:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 174:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \brief Configures the interrupt mode for each of the Pins component's
 175:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  pins. Alternatively you may set the interrupt mode for all the pins
 176:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  specified in the Pins component.
 177:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 178:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  <b>Note</b> The interrupt is port-wide and therefore any enabled pin
 179:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  interrupt may trigger it.
 180:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 181:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \param position
 182:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  The pin position as listed in the Pins component. You may OR these to be 
 183:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  able to configure the interrupt mode of multiple pins within a Pins 
 184:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  component. Or you may use VCONN_MON_P2_INTR_ALL to configure the
 185:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  interrupt mode of all the pins in the Pins component.       
 186:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  - VCONN_MON_P2_0_INTR       (First pin in the list)
 187:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  - VCONN_MON_P2_1_INTR       (Second pin in the list)
 188:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  - ...
 189:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  - VCONN_MON_P2_INTR_ALL     (All pins in Pins component)
 190:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 191:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \param mode
 192:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  Interrupt mode for the selected pins. Valid options are documented in
 193:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  \ref intrMode.
 194:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 195:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \return 
 196:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  None
 197:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  
 198:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \sideeffect
 199:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  It is recommended that the interrupt be disabled before calling this 
 200:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  function to avoid unintended interrupt requests. Note that the interrupt
 201:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  type is port wide, and therefore will trigger for any enabled pin on the 
 202:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  port.
 203:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *
 204:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** * \funcusage
 205:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *  \snippet VCONN_MON_P2_SUT.c usage_VCONN_MON_P2_SetInterruptMode
 206:.\Generated_Source\PSoC4/VCONN_MON_P2.c **** *******************************************************************************/
